    logP = -0.5);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Busulfan is an alkylating anticancer drug used to treat blood cancers such as chronic and acute myeloid leukemia, and as part of conditioning before stem cell transplantation. It remains an approved medicine, with an authorised product in the European Union, though it carries a boxed warning and is used mainly in specialist settings.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q348922&quot;>Wikidata Q348922</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>busulfan</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01AB01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01008&quot;>DB01008</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/2478&quot;>2478</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:28901&quot;>28901</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q348922&quot;>Q348922</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C6H14O6S2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>246.292 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
